150	`Cache-Control: no-store` so a cache cannot serve one after its deadline. Authenticated deletion is
151	the only operation that removes an object, is idempotent, and returns `204 No Content`:
152	
153	```bash
154	printf 'header = "Authorization: Bearer %s"\n' "$STATIC_UPLOAD_TOKEN" | \
155	  curl --config - https://www.yusoofsh.id/static/docs/guide.pdf \
156	    -X DELETE \
157	    -H "Content-Type: application/octet-stream"
158	```
159	
160	## Short links
161	
162	Short links use the same R2 bucket as static files. Create one for an existing
163	static object with the authenticated API:
164	
165	```bash
166	printf 'header = "Authorization: Bearer %s"\n' "$STATIC_UPLOAD_TOKEN" | \
167	  curl --config - https://www.yusoofsh.id/api/shortlinks \
168	    -X POST \
169	    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
170	    --data '{"path":"docs/guide.pdf"}'
171	```
172	
173	The response contains a random base62 code. Allocation starts at four
174	characters and grows only when the shorter namespace cannot find a free code:
175	
176	```json
177	{
178	  "code": "aB3x",
179	  "path": "docs/guide.pdf",
180	  "shortUrl": "https://www.yusoofsh.id/aB3x",
181	  "targetUrl": "https://www.yusoofsh.id/static/docs/guide.pdf"
182	}
183	```
184	
185	`GET` and `HEAD` requests to `/{code}` redirect publicly to the static object.
186	The generator verifies that the target already exists, so it cannot create a
187	link to a missing file. Revoke a link with the same upload token:
188	
189	```bash
190	printf 'header = "Authorization: Bearer %s"\n' "$STATIC_UPLOAD_TOKEN" | \
191	  curl --config - https://www.yusoofsh.id/api/shortlinks/aB3x \
192	    -X DELETE
193	```
194	
195	Shortlink records can include a future UTC expiration and campaign metadata:
196	
197	```json
198	{
199	  "path": "docs/guide.pdf",
200	  "expiresAt": "2099-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
201	  "campaign": {
202	    "name": "spring",
203	    "source": "newsletter",
204	    "medium": "email"
205	  }
206	}
207	```
208	
209	The target file's own expiration is authoritative: a shortlink cannot live
210	longer than its static object. Same-origin application aliases can use a
211	validated `target` path instead of `path`; external URLs and management API
212	paths are rejected:
213	
214	```json
215	{ "target": "/github?source=profile" }
216	```
217	
218	Uploads can optionally allocate a shortlink in the same response by sending
219	`X-Static-Shortlink: true`. The upload endpoint accepts the same campaign
220	headers (`X-Shortlink-Campaign`, `X-Shortlink-Source`,
221	`X-Shortlink-Medium`, and `X-Shortlink-Content`). Campaign clicks are recorded
222	by the configured `SHORTLINK_ANALYTICS` Analytics Engine binding without
223	blocking redirects; only the referrer origin is retained.
224	
225	## Analytics
226	
227	Cloudflare Web Analytics remains responsible for ordinary page views, referrer,
228	device/browser dimensions, and Web Vitals. The separate `SITE_ANALYTICS`
229	Analytics Engine binding (`leenk_site_events`) records only allowlisted custom
230	events. Each data point uses this shape:
231	
232	```text
233	blob1: event name
234	blob2: bounded dimension, when applicable
235	blob3: referrer origin only
236	double1: 1
237	index1: event name
238	```
239	
240	The current custom event taxonomy is:
241	
242	- `bio_mode_viewed` / `bio_mode_changed`: `full` or `tldr`.
243	- `content_section_viewed`: `what_i_do`, `selected_work`, or `beyond_work`.
244	- `scroll_depth_reached`: `25`, `50`, `75`, or `90` percent.
245	- `time_on_page_reached`: `10`, `30`, or `60` active seconds.
246	- `outbound_link_clicked`: `nadi`, `ydsf`, or `electgo`.
247	- `social_link_clicked`: `github`, `linkedin`, or `twitter`.
248	- `contact_link_clicked`: `email`.
249	- `internal_link_clicked`: `home` (404 recovery).
250	- `error_page_viewed`: `not_found`.
251	- `client_error`: `runtime`, `resource`, or `promise`, without messages or
252	  stack traces.
253	- `shortlink_created`: `internal` or `static`.
254	- `shortlink_deleted`: no path or code recorded in the site-events dataset.
255	- `static_file_uploaded`: `with_shortlink` or `without_shortlink`.
256	- `static_file_deleted`.
257	
258	Social networks intentionally use the single `social_link_clicked` event with
259	a bounded dimension instead of separate `github_clicked`,
260	`linkedin_clicked`, or `twitter_clicked` event names. Analytics never records
261	email addresses, account names, IP addresses, request bodies, complete URLs,
262	messages, stack traces, or other user identity. Writes are best-effort and
263	never block navigation, redirects, uploads, or deletes.
264	
265	## Deployment
266	
267	The build produces an Astro server entry point and static assets in `dist/`. Preview the exact Worker configuration locally before deploying:
268	
269	```bash
270	nub run build
271	nub run preview
272	```
273	
274	Production deployment is intentionally explicit:
275	
276	```bash
277	nub run deploy
278	```
279	
280	Deploy only after local and CI verification pass. The deploy command changes production state and requires separate approval when run by an agent.

