dependencies:
+ ctx7@0.5.7

### Writing a data point in a Worker

Source: https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-docs/blob/production/src/content/docs/analytics/analytics-engine/get-started.mdx

Example of how to call `writeDataPoint()` within a Worker's fetch handler to send data to the Analytics Engine.

```js
async fetch(request, env) {
  env.WEATHER.writeDataPoint({
    'blobs': ["Seattle", "USA", "pro_sensor_9000"], // City, State
    'doubles': [25, 0.5],
    'indexes': ["a3cd45"]
  });
  return new Response("OK!");
}
```

--------------------------------

### worker.ts

Source: https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-docs/blob/production/src/content/changelog/workers/2025-06-20-increased-blob-size-limits-in-Workers-Analytics.mdx

This snippet demonstrates writing a data point with multiple blob fields to the Workers Analytics Engine, highlighting the increased size limit.

```ts
export default {
	async fetch(request, env) {
		env.analyticsDataset.writeDataPoint({
			// The sum of all of the blob's sizes can now be 16 KB
			blobs: [
				// The URL of the request to the Worker
				request.url,
				// Some metadata about your application you'd like to store
				JSON.stringify(metadata),
				// The version of your Worker this datapoint was collected from
				env.versionMetadata.tag,
			],
			indexes: ["sample-index"],
		});
	}
};
```

--------------------------------

### Write Aggregated Metrics to Analytics Engine from a Tail Worker

Source: https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-docs/blob/production/src/content/docs/workers/observability/logs/tail-workers.mdx

This snippet demonstrates how a `tail()` handler can process incoming log events and write aggregated data points to the `ANALYTICS` binding. It counts events and categorizes them by script name, outcome, and Cloudflare colo.

```js
export default {
	async tail(events, env) {
		for (const event of events) {
			env.ANALYTICS.writeDataPoint({
				blobs: [event.scriptName, event.outcome],
				doubles: [1],
				indexes: [event.event?.request?.cf?.colo ?? "unknown"]
			});
		}
	}
};
```

### Limits

Source: https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-docs/blob/production/src/content/docs/analytics/analytics-engine/limits.mdx

The following limits apply to Workers Analytics Engine: Analytics Engine will accept up to twenty blobs, twenty doubles, and one index per call to `writeDataPoint`. The total size of all blobs in a request must not exceed 16 KB. The 16 KB size limit for the blobs field applies to each individual data point, regardless of how many are included in a single request using writeDataPoints(). Each index must not be more than 96 bytes. You can write a maximum of 250 data points per Worker invocation (client HTTP request). Each call to `writeDataPoint` counts towards this limit.

--------------------------------

### workers_analytics_engine > Key Points

Source: https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-docs/blob/production/src/content/partials/prompts/base-prompt.txt

- Binds an Analytics Engine dataset to the Worker
- Uses the `AnalyticsEngineDataset` type when using TypeScript for the binding
- Writes event data using the `writeDataPoint` method and writes an `AnalyticsEngineDataPoint`
- Does NOT `await` calls to `writeDataPoint`, as it is non-blocking
- Defines an index as the key representing an app, customer, merchant or tenant.
- Developers can use the GraphQL or SQL APIs to query data written to Analytics Engine

