raw_content:
Progress! The dual-effect crash is gone. New failure: during the build, the workerd prerender step failed with "No such module 'node:module'" in the user-worker — the SSR bundle was built but when run in workerd for prerendering, `node:module` isn't available. This is the prerender step: the integration's workerd prerender environment runs prerendered pages in workerd, and something in the bundle imports `node:module` (probably from @astrojs/react or the vite plugin or our code?). The vite config's rollupOptions.external includes node:* modules — with the local adapter config, these externals apply; the workerd prerender needs nodejs_compat enabled to provide node:module. The integration adds nodejs_compat automatically at deploy (per the docs: "nodejs_compat is always included in the Worker's compatibility flags") — but for the LOCAL build, the plugin's worker config (compatibility flags) defaults may not include nodejs_compat.

The fix: pass `vite.worker.compatibilityFlags` (or similar) to distilledCloudflare() in astro.config.local.ts. Let me check the CloudflareVitePluginOptions shape for compatibility flags: `worker: { compatibilityDate, compatibilityFlags, ... }`. So:

```ts
distilledCloudflare({
  vite: {
    worker: {
      compatibilityDate: "2026-07-13",
      compatibilityFlags: ["nodejs_compat"],
    },
  },
})
```

Wait — the CloudflareVitePluginOptions: earlier source.ts type: `CloudflareVitePluginOptions["worker"]` includes bindings etc. Let me check the vite plugin's option shape: `distilledCloudflare({ vite: { worker: { ... } } })`. Let me check the d.ts of @distilled.cloud/cloudflare-vite-plugin for the worker config keys (compatibilityDate, compatibilityFlags, name...).

Also the prerender: default prerenderEnvironment "workerd" — could switch to "node" to avoid workerd prerender, but the local build then uses node prerender which is closer to how CI builds. Actually for CI verification, `prerenderEnvironment: "node"` is simpler and matches old @astrojs/cloudflare behavior (astro's stock node prerenderer). Hmm — but node prerender may fail on cloudflare-specific imports. The site has no prerendered pages? Pages: index.astro is SSR (islands), 404, github/linkedin/twitter redirects — these might be prerendered? [code].ts, api routes are SSR. index.astro — does it have `export const prerender`? Not seen. So maybe NOTHING is prerendered, and the workerd prerender step shouldn't run... but it did (the error came from the prerender environment "user-worker"). The vite plugin prerenders statically-exported pages. 404.astro might be prerendered by default in Astro 7? (404 handling). The error: "Check the configuration for service 'user-worker'" — that's the prerender worker.

Two options:
1. Add nodejs_compat to the local config's worker flags (mirrors production, keeps workerd prerender).
2. Set prerenderEnvironment: "node".

Option 1 is most faithful. Let me check the vite plugin's worker option type.

