`AstroUserConfig` lives at `astro/dist/types/public/config.d.ts` — the "types" export (`astro/types`). So `import type { AstroUserConfig } from "astro/types"` should work. Use that annotation on baseConfig to prevent widening:

```ts
import type { AstroUserConfig } from "astro/types";
export const baseConfig: AstroUserConfig = {...};
```

Note: baseConfig typed as AstroUserConfig, then defineConfig(baseConfig) is fine, and spreading into local config keeps literal types (since the spread source is typed). Let me apply.

