raw_content:
TypeScript 7's deep generic comparison chokes on `Parameters<typeof defineConfig>[0]` (AstroUserConfig with 3 generics — excessive stack depth). This is a TS7 limitation with the satisfies-style deep check.

Different approach: skip the annotation entirely and make the local config NOT spread baseConfig. Duplicate the config in astro.config.local.ts explicitly (it's a small file) — simple and avoids all typing pain:

astro.config.local.ts:
```ts
import { distilledCloudflare } from "@distilled.cloud/astro/cloudflare";
import react from "@astrojs/react";
import tailwindcss from "@tailwindcss/vite";
import { defineConfig } from "astro/config";
import path from "path";

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [react(), distilledCloudflare({ vite: { compatibilityDate: "2026-07-11", compatibilityFlags: ["nodejs_compat"] } })],
  output: "server",
  site: "https://www.yusoofsh.id/",
  vite: { build: {...}, plugins: [tailwindcss()], resolve: { alias: { "~": path.resolve("./src") } } },
});
```

And astro.config.ts keeps its own object without the baseConfig export (no annotation). Duplication of ~25 lines — acceptable and explicit; the comment explains both must stay in sync. Drop `baseConfig` export entirely.

This also resolves the "Excessive stack depth" error by removing the cross-file typing.

