My worker-configuration.d.ts change broke the Env type resolution: `import { env } from "cloudflare:workers"` — the `env` variable's type comes from... the `cloudflare:workers` module declaration, which likely references the `Cloudflare.Env` interface (from @cloudflare/workers-types: `declare namespace Cloudflare { interface Env }`). The original file declared BOTH `namespace Cloudflare { interface Env extends __BaseEnv_Env }` AND `interface Env extends __BaseEnv_Env`. I removed the Cloudflare namespace declaration. The cloudflare:workers module probably types env as `Cloudflare.Env`. Restore that shape:

```ts
interface __BaseEnv_Env {
  STATIC_FILES: R2Bucket;
  SHORTLINK_ANALYTICS: AnalyticsEngineDataset;
  SITE_ANALYTICS: AnalyticsEngineDataset;
  CMS?: D1Database;
  CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID?: string;
  CLOUDFLARE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN?: string;
  STATIC_UPLOAD_TOKEN?: string;
}
declare namespace Cloudflare {
  interface Env extends __BaseEnv_Env {}
}
interface Env extends __BaseEnv_Env {}
```

