raw_content:
The Policy output has `policyId` but the RESOURCE call returns an Effect (like other resources) — the docs example: `const allowMyOrg = yield* Cloudflare.Access.Policy("AllowMyOrg", {...}); ... policies: [allowMyOrg.policyId]` — the policy must be YIELDED first. The docs show `yield*` in the stack effect. So `OwnerPolicy` needs to be declared as a resource description and yielded inside the stack, then passed to the Application props. But Application props are declared at module scope... The Application props take `policies: ReadonlyArray<string | ...>` — the policyId. To reference the yielded policy inside module-scope Application props, use a props Effect that yields the policy:

```ts
const OwnerPolicy = Cloudflare.Access.Policy("OwnerPolicy", {...});

const DashboardApp = Cloudflare.Access.Application(
  "DashboardApp",
  Effect.gen(function* () {
    const ownerPolicy = yield* OwnerPolicy;
    return { type: "self_hosted", name: "leenk - dashboard", domain: "www.yusoofsh.id/dashboard", policies: [ownerPolicy.policyId] };
  }),
);
```

That works: props Eff can yield other resources (they get deployed through the dependency graph). Let me apply.

