raw_content:
Two lint errors:
1. cms.ts:35 — `\[` in the regex character class `[^\[\]]` — inside a character class, escaping `[` is unnecessary. Replace `[^\[\]]` with `[^\[\]]` → `[^[\]]`? Actually within a character class: `[^\[\]]` — the `\[` and `\]` inside the class: `]` needs escaping in some contexts; oxlint says `\[` is unnecessary. Use `[^[\]]`. Hmm — `]` right after `[^` — to be safe use `[^\]\[]`? oxlint flags only `\[`. Change `[^\[\]]{1,128}` → `[^[\]]{1,128}`. Wait, does `]` inside the class need escaping? In JS regex, `]` inside a character class must be escaped unless it's the first character after `[` or `[^`. `[^[\]]` — the class is `[^...]`: contents `[` `\]` — `]` escaped — fine. So `[^[\]]{1,128}`.
2. homepage-render.ts:93 — the destructured `const [, label, kind, target] = match;` then `(kind ?? "url") as CmsLinkKind` — same unsafe assertion. Match groups are `string | undefined`; the pattern guarantees one of the four kinds. Fix like cms.ts: validate via isCmsLinkKind (import it) or construct differently. Simplest: reuse a helper from cms.ts: export a `parseInlineLinkMatch`? Or in renderInlineText, since validation already happened at save time, just default: `const kindValue = kind ?? "url"; if (!isCmsLinkKind(kindValue)) { render as plain escaped text }` — import isCmsLinkKind from cms. Actually renderInlineLink receives kind typed CmsLinkKind; change call site: build kind via isCmsLinkKind check, skipping the token (rendering it as escaped literal text) if invalid:

```ts
const [, label, kind, target] = match;
const kindValue = kind ?? "url";
if (!isCmsLinkKind(kindValue)) {
  result += escapeHtml(match[0]);
  lastIndex = index + match[0].length;
  continue;
}
result += renderInlineLink(label ?? "", kindValue, target ?? "");
```

Import isCmsLinkKind in homepage-render.

